From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:21:32 -0643
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zumapro: Add Trusty

Describe Trusty, the secure OS the bootloader starts, as on gs201: its
IPIs are GIC SGIs 8 to 15. It stays disabled. The GSA starts the AoC
through Trusty's hwmgr service, so audio and sensors need it.

Booted on the Pixel 9a:
7.3.0-rc6-omamobile-tegu-s2mpg15-m1-g991042e2eff3-dirty has this node,
enabled by an overlay at runtime; trusty-core, -log, -ipc and -virtio
bind it and the GSA reaches its hwmgr port.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi
index 8fac5f8ab..3ba0b68c0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi
@@ -594,6 +594,26 @@ map0 {
 		};
 	};
 
+	/* Trusty, the secure OS that runs from the bootloader's tzsw image. */
+	trusty: trusty {
+		compatible = "android,trusty-smc-v1";
+		status = "disabled";
+
+		irq {
+			compatible = "android,trusty-irq-v1";
+			/* Trusty IPIs 8-15 are GIC SGIs 8-15 */
+			ipi-range = <8 15 8>;
+		};
+
+		log {
+			compatible = "android,trusty-log-v1";
+		};
+
+		virtio {
+			compatible = "android,trusty-virtio-v1";
+		};
+	};
+
 	soc: soc {
 		compatible = "simple-bus";
 		#address-cells = <2>;
